#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/deriving-traits.md:17
msgid ""
"// Many traits have simple implementations that can be generated "
"automatically.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/deriving-traits.md:31
msgid ""
"Many traits have trivial implementations that would be easy to mechanically "
"write. For these traits, it's possible to have the compiler generate the "
"implementation for us using a derive macro."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/deriving-traits.md:35
msgid ""
"For example, the `Clone` trait is commonly implemented by simply cloning all "
"fields of the struct. If this is the behavior we want for our type, we don't "
"need to write out the boilerplate ourselves. Replace the manual "
"implementation with the corresponding derive."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/deriving-traits.md:40
msgid ""
"Derived trait implementations automatically stay in sync with your type "
"definition. Demonstrate adding a field to `DrawingBuffer` and show that the "
"derived `Clone` impl is automatically updated, whereas the manual impl has "
"to be updated by hand."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/deriving-traits.md:45
msgid ""
"Many standard library traits support being derived, and it's common for "
"traits defined in the ecosystem to also support this."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/deriving-traits.md:48
msgid ""
"Traits do not support being derived by default, but you can implement derive "
"support for your own traits with a macro. Doing so is covered in the Macros "
"course."
msgstr ""

